problem:
A sequence of positive integers \( a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots \) is defined as follows:
\[ a_{n+1} = 
\begin{cases} 
3a_n + 1 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is odd} \\
\frac{a_n}{2} & \text{if } a_n \text{ is even}
\end{cases}
\]
Given that \( a_1 = 7 \), find the smallest positive integer \( k \) such that \( a_k = 1 \).

Find the number of ordered pairs \((x,y)\) that satisfy the system of equations
\begin{align*}
x^4 + y^4 &= 18 \\
x^2 + y^2 &= 6
\end{align*}
and verify that no real solutions exist by analyzing the discriminant of the resulting quadratic equation.

A semicircle of radius \( r \) is inscribed in a triangle with one side equal to \( 2r \). What is the maximum possible area of such a triangle? [asy]
unitsize(2cm);
defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10));
dotfactor = 4;
draw(arc((1/2,0),1/2,0,180)--cycle);
draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1/2,1/2*sqrt(3))--cycle);
label("$A$", (0,0), SW);
label("$B$", (1,0), SE);
label("$C$", (1/2,1/2*sqrt(3)), N);
dot((1/2,0));
dot((1/2,1/2*sqrt(3)));
[/asy]

A sequence of positive integers \(a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots\) is defined by \(a_1 = 2\) and for \(n \geq 1\),
\[a_{n+1} = \begin{cases} 
3a_n + 1 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is odd} \\
\frac{a_n}{2} & \text{if } a_n \text{ is even}
\end{cases}\]
What is the smallest positive integer \(k\) such that \(a_k = a_{k+3}\)?

What is the sum of the measures, in degrees, of the indicated angles in the given geometric diagram?

In the diagram, the four straight lines $BF$, $CG$, $DH$, and $AD$ are intersecting at point $A$. There are three angles marked as $x$, $y$, and $z$ around point $A$.

Find the value of $x + y + z$.

