What is the minimum value of \[
\left( \frac{\left(\left(-2\right) \cdot a + 3 \cdot b - 5 \cdot c + 2 \cdot d\right)^2}{405}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}
\] where $a,b,c,d$ are any real numbers and $a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2 = 2$? Express your answer in the simplest form.

Find the number of ordered pairs $(x, y)$ of real numbers such that
\begin{align*}
x^2 + y^2 - 2x + 2y &= 0,\\
x^2 - y^2 + 4x - 4y &= 0.
\end{align*}

Consider a sequence of positive integers \( a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots \) defined by \( a_1 = 1 \) and for \( n \geq 1 \), 
\[ a_{n+1} = \begin{cases} 
2a_n & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \\
\left\lfloor \sqrt{a_n} \right\rfloor & \text{if } n \text{ is even}
\end{cases} \]

Determine the value of \( a_{2024} \).

Suppose $f(x)$ is a real function defined for all $x \in \mathbb{R}$, with the following properties:
(1) $f(1) = 0$;
(2) $f(xy) + 1 = f(x) + y$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{R}$;
(3) there exist real numbers $a$ and $b$ such that $f(a) = f(b) = 1$.
Find the value of $a + b$.

A semicircle of diameter 1 sits at the top of a semicircle of diameter 2, as shown. Determine the area of the shaded region.

[asy]
import graph;
fill((2.45,0)..(2-sin(50),cos(50))..cycle,gray(0.7));
fill((2.45,0)..(2+sin(50),-cos(50))..cycle,gray(0.7));
draw((0,0)..(2,0)..cycle);
draw((2,0)..(3,0)..(3,2)..(1,2)..(1,0)..cycle);
[/asy]

There are 3 types of cards, A, B, and C. Cards of type A and B both have 1 dot, while cards of type C have 2 dots. From an unlimited supply of these cards, five cards are selected at random and stacked one on top of another, resulting in a "card tower." The "height" of a card tower is the sum of the number of dots on the five cards. For example, the card tower shown in the figure below has a height of 3 and is denoted by (A, B, C).

[asy]
size(120);
void drawcard(pair a, string s) {
draw((a+(0,1))--(a--(a+(1,0))--(a+(1,1))), linewidth(1.1));
label(String(s), a+(0.5,0.5), fontsize(13pt));
}
drawcard((0,2), "A");
drawcard((1,2), "B");
drawcard((2,2), "C");
drawcard((3,2), "C");
drawcard((4,2), "C");
[/asy]

How many different card towers with a height of 8 are possible?

(A) 10
(B) 24
(C) 42
(D) 60
(E) 96

Hint: It is possible to choose more than one card of each type to build the card tower.

The answer is 60

Let \( f(x) \) be a polynomial function such that for any positive integer \( n \),
\[ f(n) = \begin{cases} 
1 & \text{if } n \text{ is a perfect square,} \\
0 & \text{otherwise.} 
\end{cases} \]
Find the sum of all coefficients of \( f(x) \) if it is known that \( f(x) \) has a degree of 2023.

Consider a sequence of positive integers \( a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots \) defined recursively by \( a_1 = 1 \) and for \( n \geq 1 \), 

$$
a_{n+1} = \begin{cases} 
a_n + 1 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is even} \\
3a_n + 1 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is odd} 
\end{cases}
$$

Determine the smallest positive integer \( k \) such that \( a_k \geq 2024 \).

