A sequence of positive integers $a_1, a_2, a_3, \dots$ is defined recursively by $a_1 = 2$ and for all $n \geq 1$, \[a_{n+1} = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
a_n + 3 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is divisible by } 3 \\
2a_n - 1 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is not divisible by } 3
\end{array}
\right.\] Find the remainder when $a_{2023}$ is divided by $1000$.

Let \( S \) be the set of all positive integers. Find the number of functions \( f : S \to S \) satisfying the following properties:
(i) \( f(x) + f(y) \) is divisible by \( f(x + y) \) for all \( x, y \in S \);
(ii) for any finite increasing sequence \( x_1, x_2, \ldots, x_n \) in \( S \), there exists a positive integer \( t \leq n \) such that \( f(x_1 + x_2 + \cdots + x_t) \) is not divisible by \( x_1 + x_2 + \cdots + x_t \).
